.TH SOPHIA 1 "May 2026" "Sophia 0.1.0" "SOPHIA Manual"
.SH NAME
sophia \- a modern, TUI-based replacement for the classic ping command
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B sophia
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fITARGET\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B sophia
is a high-performance terminal UI ping tool optimized for macOS. It provides a real-time dashboard displaying latency charts and network statistics.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i, \-\-interval " <MILLISECONDS>"
The interval between ICMP echo requests. Default is 1000ms.
.TP
.BI \-t, \-\-timeout " <MILLISECONDS>"
The time to wait for a response before marking it as a drop. Default is 1000ms.
.TP
.BI \-h, \-\-help
Print help information.
.TP
.BI \-V, \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
.TP
.B 1, 2, 3, 4
Switch between Dashboard, Chart, Log, and Stats view modes.
.TP
.B F1
Toggle the interactive help menu.
.TP
.B q
Quit the application and restore the terminal state.
.TP
.B Esc
Close the help menu if open.
.TP
.B Ctrl+C
Forcefully exit the application and restore the terminal state.
.SH SECURITY
SOPHIA is written in 100% safe Rust and prioritizes unprivileged ICMP sockets (DGRAM). If system permissions prevent raw socket access, SOPHIA will report the error. Running with
.B sudo
may be required on some systems if unprivileged ICMP is disabled.
